 watch and held the line\nwith brothers, sisters at her side.\nThe flag is folded, Taps is played,\nthe last salute is slowly made;\nthe watch is over. Rest, and know\nthat what you gave will never fade.\nWritten for this card","align":"c","ls":1.18,"font":"LAi","size":9.6,"color":"#2C3650","spc":0.0,"prose":{"font":"LA","size":10.2,"color":"#2C3650","ls":1.3,"after":6.12},"poem":{"font":"LAi","size":9.6,"color":"#2C3650","ls":1.18,"stanza":5.28},"source":{"font":"LAi","size":8,"color":"#5F6882","ls":1.0,"before":5.6}},{"t":"text","bind":"in_memory","x":0.38,"y":4.78,"w":3.24,"h":0.1562,"anchor":"m","sample":"In honored memory of","align":"c","ls":1.0,"font":"LAi","size":9.0,"color":"#5F6882","spc":0.0},{"t":"text","bind":"name","x":0.38,"y":4.9562,"w":3.24,"h":0.2456,"anchor":"m","sample":"Lt. Eleanor Grace Whitfield","align":"c","ls":0.95,"font":"PF","size":13.0,"color":"#1E2A44","spc":0.0},{"t":"text","bind":"dates","x":0.38,"y":5.2218,"w":3.24,"h":0.1892,"anchor":"m","sample":"March 4, 1941 – September 12, 2026","align":"c","ls":1.1,"font":"LA","size":8.6,"color":"#2C3650","spc":0.2}],"bg":"cm-bg-veteran-46-vet_patriot-back.jpg","px":[1200,1800]}],"vet_sky":[{"design":"vet_sky","side":"front","w":4.0,"h":6.0,"els":[{"t":"text","bind":"kicker","x":0.2,"y":0.36,"w":3.6,"h":0.62,"anchor":"m","sample":"Fair Winds and Following Seas","align":"c","ls":1.0,"font":"GV","size":15.89,"color":"#2E5A8E","spc":0.0},{"t":"photo","bind":"photo","x":0.85,"y":1.06,"w":2.3,"h":2.8111,"border":"#5E86B8","bw":1.0},{"t":"text","bind":"name","x":0.35,"y":4.0111,"w":3.3,"h":0.62,"anchor":"m","sample":"Sgt. Robert James Carter","align":"c","ls":0.92,"font":"PF","size":19.0,"color":"#1F3450","spc":0.0},{"t":"text","bind":"dates","x":0.35,"y":4.6911,"w":3.3,"h":0.21,"anchor":"m","sample":"June 12, 1948 – September 10, 2026","align":"c","ls":1.15,"font":"LA","size":9.5,"color":"#2B3A4F","spc":0.2}],"bg":"cm-bg-veteran-46-vet_sky-front.jpg","px":[1200,1800]},{"design":"vet_sky","side":"back","w":4.0,"h":6.0,"els":[{"t":"text","bind":"verse_title","x":0.2,"y":0.76,"w":3.6,"h":0.36,"anchor":"m","sample":"Eternal Father, Strong to Save","align":"c","ls":1.0,"font":"PF","size":15.0,"color":"#2E5A8E","spc":0.0},{"t":"verse","bind":"verse","x":0.38,"y":1.18,"w":3.24,"h":3.5,"anchor":"m","sample":"Eternal Father, strong to save,\nwhose arm hath bound the restless wave,\nwho bidd’st the mighty ocean deep\nits own appointed limits keep;\nO hear us when we cry to Thee\nfor those in peril on the sea.\nO Trinity of love and power,\nour brethren shield in danger’s hour;\nfrom rock and tempest, fire and foe,\nprotect them wheresoe’er they go;\nthus evermore shall rise to Thee\nglad hymns of praise from land and sea.\nWilliam Whiting, 1860 (the Navy Hymn)","align":"c","ls":1.18,"font":"LAi","size":9.6,"color":"#2B3A4F","spc":0.0,"prose":{"font":"LA","size":10.2,"color":"#2B3A4F","ls":1.3,"after":6.12},"poem":{"font":"LAi","size":9.6,"color":"#2B3A4F","ls":1.18,"stanza":5.28},"source":{"font":"LAi","size":8,"color":"#5D6D80","ls":1.0,"before":5.6}},{"t":"text","bind":"in_memory","x":0.38,"y":4.78,"w":3.24,"h":0.1562,"anchor":"m","sample":"In honored memory of","align":"c","ls":1.0,"font":"LAi","size":9.0,"color":"#5D6D80","spc":0.0},{"t":"text","bind":"name","x":0.38,"y":4.9562,"w":3.24,"h":0.2456,"anchor":"m","sample":"Sgt. Robert James Carter","align":"c","ls":0.95,"font":"PF","size":13.0,"color":"#1F3450","spc":0.0},{"t":"text","bind":"dates","x":0.38,"y":5.2218,"w":3.24,"h":0.1892,"anchor":"m","sample":"June 12, 1948 – September 10, 2026","align":"c","ls":1.1,"font":"LA","size":8.6,"color":"#2B3A4F","spc":0.2}],"bg":"cm-bg-veteran-46-vet_sky-back.jpg","px":[1200,1800]}],"vet_olive":[{"design":"vet_olive","side":"front","w":4.0,"h":6.0,"els":[{"t":"text","bind":"kicker","x":0.2,"y":0.36,"w":3.6,"h":0.62,"anchor":"m","sample":"Rest Easy","align":"c","ls":1.0,"font":"GV","size":28.89,"color":"#5F7249","spc":0.0},{"t":"photo","bind":"photo","x":0.85,"y":1.06,"w":2.3,"h":2.8111,"border":"#8A9A6A","bw":1.0},{"t":"text","bind":"name","x":0.35,"y":4.0111,"w":3.3,"h":0.62,"anchor":"m","sample":"Lt. Eleanor Grace Whitfield","align":"c","ls":0.92,"font":"PF","size":19.0,"color":"#2F3A2C","spc":0.0},{"t":"text","bind":"dates","x":0.35,"y":4.6911,"w":3.3,"h":0.21,"anchor":"m","sample":"March 4, 1941 – September 12, 2026","align":"c","ls":1.15,"font":"LA","size":9.5,"color":"#343E32","spc":0.2}],"bg":"cm-bg-veteran-46-vet_olive-front.jpg","px":[1200,1800]},{"design":"vet_olive","side":"back","w":4.0,"h":6.0,"els":[{"t":"text","bind":"verse_title","x":0.2,"y":0.76,"w":3.6,"h":0.36,"anchor":"m","sample":"The Twenty-Third Psalm","align":"c","ls":1.0,"font":"PF","size":15.0,"color":"#5A6B45","spc":0.0},{"t":"verse","bind":"verse","x":0.38,"y":1.18,"w":3.24,"h":3.5,"anchor":"m","sample":"The Lord is my shepherd; I shall not want. He maketh me to lie down in green pastures: he leadeth me beside the still waters. He restoreth my soul: he leadeth me in the paths of righteousness for his name’s sake. Yea, though I walk through the valley of the shadow of death, I will fear no evil: for thou art with me; thy rod and thy staff they comfort me. Thou preparest a table before me in the presence of mine enemies: thou anointest my head with oil; my cup runneth over. Surely goodness and mercy shall follow me all the days of my life: and I will dwell in the house of the Lord for ever.\nPsalm 23, King James Version","align":"c","ls":1.3,"font":"LA","size":10.2,"color":"#343E32","spc":0.0,"prose":{"font":"LA","size":10.2,"color":"#343E32","ls":1.3,"after":6.12},"poem":{"font":"LAi","size":9.6,"color":"#343E32","ls":1.18,"stanza":5.28},"source":{"font":"LAi","size":8,"color":"#68725E","ls":1.0,"before":5.6}},{"t":"text","bind":"in_memory","x":0.38,"y":4.78,"w":3.24,"h":0.1562,"anchor":"m","sample":"In honored memory of","align":"c","ls":1.0,"font":"LAi","size":9.0,"color":"#68725E","spc":0.0},{"t":"text","bind":"name","x":0.38,"y":4.9562,"w":3.24,"h":0.2456